\p{Filed under [[conf-neuromod-nyc-2026]]. A modeling companion to the Minnesota traveling-wave work ([[conf-umn-twtacs]]).}

\image{conf-umn-multiscale-circuit.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} A biophysical, \strong{multiscale cortical-circuit} model that couples microscopic transmembrane currents to the \strong{macroscopic scalp voltages} you actually record — a realistic-head FEM feeding a laminar circuit so simulated scalp EEG has a mechanistic generator. Aimed at making NIBS dose-response in motor cortex (and non-motor targets by frontal geometry) target-specific and electric-field-informed, rather than nominal. The generative bridge between the fast single-unit solves ([[conf-neuromodec-hh-operators]]) and network-scale readouts.}
